{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Operator-approved scope\nImplement the finalized 2026-09-02 scope from the ticket comments: rebar LLM gate operations emit lightweight keepalive lines synchronously at existing progress seams so supervising stall watchdogs are not silent for an entire multi-call gate phase.\n\n## Implementation plan\n1. Add a small shared LLM keepalive helper with a module-level interval constant (~20-30 seconds) and a single last-emit-timestamp comparison. It logs at WARNING so the line reaches stderr at rebar's default effective log level (WARNING) without `REBAR_LOG_LEVEL`.\n2. Emit through that helper at the primary per-LLM-call seam in `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, including operation/phase name, call index when available, and elapsed seconds only.\n3. Ensure keepalive content excludes prompt text, model responses, tool arguments, and tool payloads.\n4. Emit through the same helper at tool-call boundaries in `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py`.\n5. Emit through the same helper at workflow-step boundaries in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py`.\n6. Use the shared elapsed-time coalescing so bursts of fast tool/step calls do not produce one line per call.\n7. Keep the change purely additive: no background daemon thread, no progress-gating/stall escalation/health withdrawal, no total-runtime cap, and no change to existing timeout behavior, preserving ADR 0089.\n8. Add a short warning to gate documentation that gate ops can exceed common 600s supervisor stall budgets while silent between calls; the new keepalive mitigates multi-call silence, but a single very long request can still exceed a budget. Note `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_S=600` is per request and close can make many requests, so supervisors may need larger no-output budgets.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Default-level keepalive: a gate/agentic-loop path crossing per-call progress emits at least one keepalive line to stderr/log capture at the default WARNING level. Verified by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_keepalive.py::test_runner_keepalive_reaches_default_warning_level -q`.\n- [ ] Coalescing: rapid tool-call/step bursts do not emit one line per call. Verified by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_keepalive.py::test_tool_keepalives_are_coalesced -q`.\n- [ ] Content safety: keepalive lines include only operation/phase name, call index where available, and elapsed seconds. Verified by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_keepalive.py -q`.\n- [ ] ADR 0089 compatibility: no timer thread, total-runtime cap, timeout change, or interruption of slow-but-alive calls is introduced. Verified by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py::test_no_total_runtime_timer_mechanism tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py::test_slow_but_alive_server_completes_under_read_timeout -q`.\n- [ ] Documentation: the supervisor stall-budget warning lands in the gate/config docs. Verified by review of `docs/plan-review-gate.md` and/or `docs/config.md` plus `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`.\n\n## Testing\nTargeted RED/GREEN commands:\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_keepalive.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py::test_no_total_runtime_timer_mechanism tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py::test_slow_but_alive_server_completes_under_read_timeout -q`\n\nReview preflight commands:\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n\nEmpirical default-level check:\n- Run a fast deterministic gate/runner invocation without `REBAR_LOG_LEVEL` and assert the keepalive is written through logging at WARNING, which reaches stderr/log capture under the default effective level.\n\n## Portability\nThe implementation is pure Python logging plus deterministic unit tests. It does not depend on any CI provider, external daemon, terminal feature, or platform-specific supervisor, satisfying project portability."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788383681283555304,"uuid":"b9db5ee3-456f-47a7-8913-b34cd681a946"}